VITEUI – HARD RULES
Project Scope

viteui is a client-focused project.
The goal is to abandon Gradio and the original WebUI frontend and instead:
Wrap the original Forge (WebUI) API

Build the UI entirely with Vite
located in: client/src/

This is a hybrid project:
Original Forge code is kept only to:
Pull upstream improvements

Maintain compatibility with extensions

Support future Forge/WebUI changes

Original Forge Code (READ-ONLY)
The untouched reference copy of Forge lives in:
original-forge/
This folder is FOR REFERENCE ONLY.

🚫 NEVER modify, run, or depend on the following files or paths:
launch.py
launch_utils.py
webui*.bat
webui*.py
webui*.sh
viteui does not use these files at runtime.
ViteUI Fork Rules

Every new or modified file in the viteui fork OUTSIDE of client/|modules_viteapi/ MUST start with:# VITE UI

Modifying Forge Code (LAST RESORT)
Only if absolutely unavoidable, you may touch code inside:/modules//modules_forge//extensions-builtin//extensions//backend//scripts/
When this happens:
Changes must be minimal

Logic must be handled externally via:/viteui-gradio/(e.g. wrappers, adapters, shims)
Required Modification Markup

Any change to original Forge code MUST use one of the following formats.
Removing code; we keep the code but comment it out. Explain why we are removing it.
#? explanation for following removal
#- removed line
#- removed line
#?end

Adding code
#+ explanation for following addition
added line
added line
#+end

🚫 No unannotated edits
🚫 No refactors
🚫 No stylistic changes

Client Testing

To test client-side changes without conflicts, always run:
cd client
npm run dev --port 5174